#. Key:	149315438
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Packs/Frontier/Minigames/Poker/UI/WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection.WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection_C:WidgetTree.NameLabel.Text
#: /Game/Packs/Frontier/Minigames/Poker/UI/WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection.WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection_C:WidgetTree.NameLabel.Text
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,149315438"
msgid "A highly competitive tournament version of Poker.\r\nPlayers sit down and wager any Items they want in a long-form tournament-style game. All players must agree to wagered Items before the game begins. Blinds increase as the game goes on, and play continues until one player wins all the chips. The winning player keeps all the wagered Items."
msgstr "A highly competitive tournament version of Poker.\r\nPlayers sit down and wager any Items they want in a long-form tournament-style game. All players must agree to wagered Items before the game begins. Blinds increase as the game goes on, and play continues until one player wins all the chips. The winning player keeps all the wagered Items."

#. Key:	130291518
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/Packs/Frontier/Minigames/Poker/UI/WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection.WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection_C:WidgetTree.NameLabel_1.Text
#: /Game/Packs/Frontier/Minigames/Poker/UI/WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection.WBP_PAA_GameTypeSelection_C:WidgetTree.NameLabel_1.Text
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,130291518"
msgid "A more casual version of Poker where players may come and go.\r\nPlayers may only buy-in with the table's pre-selected Item type. Each copy of that Item \"purchases\" chips from the table, which can be used to play. Blinds never increase, and players may come and go as they wish. When a player leaves the table, they exchange their chips for the table's pre-determined Item."
msgstr "A more casual version of Poker where players may come and go.\r\nPlayers may only buy-in with the table's pre-selected Item type. Each copy of that Item \"purchases\" chips from the table, which can be used to play. Blinds never increase, and players may come and go as they wish. When a player leaves the table, they exchange their chips for the table's pre-determined Item."

