#. Key:	3387491624
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(162).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(162).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "Content,3387491624"
msgid "Common name:\nTusoteuthis\nSpecies: Tusoteuthis vampyrus\nTime: Cretaceous\nDiet: Carnivore\nTemperament: Aggressive\n\nWild\nTusoteuthis vampyrus is a very aggressive water predator. Approximately 30 feet long, Tusoteuthis is a terror of the deep. Once it grabs its prey, it slowly crushes it into submission while using the talons on its tentacles to siphon and drink the victim's blood!\n\nTusoteuthis is a terrifying opponent for several reasons. Firstly, its grab slowly renders its victim unconscious, so death isn't the only concern. Secondly, its vampiric blood drain instantly revitalizes it, even during combat. Finally, if Tusoteuthis is losing the fight, it sprays a cloud of ink into the surrounding water, blinding its attackers to cover a sneaky escape.\n\nDomesticated\nOne of the major benefits of taming Tusoteuthis is harvesting its ink. Unlike normal ink, Tusoteuthis' ink is very oily, and can even be refined into fuels such as gasoline. Between that and Tusoteuthis' distinctive capability to grab & carry large creatures underwater, it makes for an excellent aquatic tame, despite its slower speed."
msgstr "Common name:\nTusoteuthis\nSpecies: Tusoteuthis vampyrus\nTime: Cretaceous\nDiet: Carnivore\nTemperament: Aggressive\n\nWild\nTusoteuthis vampyrus is a very aggressive water predator. Approximately 30 feet long, Tusoteuthis is a terror of the deep. Once it grabs its prey, it slowly crushes it into submission while using the talons on its tentacles to siphon and drink the victim's blood!\n\nTusoteuthis is a terrifying opponent for several reasons. Firstly, its grab slowly renders its victim unconscious, so death isn't the only concern. Secondly, its vampiric blood drain instantly revitalizes it, even during combat. Finally, if Tusoteuthis is losing the fight, it sprays a cloud of ink into the surrounding water, blinding its attackers to cover a sneaky escape.\n\nDomesticated\nOne of the major benefits of taming Tusoteuthis is harvesting its ink. Unlike normal ink, Tusoteuthis' ink is very oily, and can even be refined into fuels such as gasoline. Between that and Tusoteuthis' distinctive capability to grab & carry large creatures underwater, it makes for an excellent aquatic tame, despite its slower speed."

#. Key:	2241023675
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(168).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(168).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "Content,2241023675"
msgid "Well, I found the reports on Mister Nerva to be rather exaggerated, and as an Englishman, one might imagine that I'd view Roman leadership with some disdain. Yet, in my experience, I found Mister Nerva to be civil, honest and intellectually engaging.\nIn fact, after a lengthy conversation, I daresay that Mister Nerva has the right of it when it comes to this island's politics. As the Romans created Pax Romana, perhaps this New Legion will create Pax Arcam. Even if it doesn't, I doubt it will harm my research, so I see no reason to interfere in this particular squabble."
msgstr "Well, I found the reports on Mister Nerva to be rather exaggerated, and as an Englishman, one might imagine that I'd view Roman leadership with some disdain. Yet, in my experience, I found Mister Nerva to be civil, honest and intellectually engaging.\nIn fact, after a lengthy conversation, I daresay that Mister Nerva has the right of it when it comes to this island's politics. As the Romans created Pax Romana, perhaps this New Legion will create Pax Arcam. Even if it doesn't, I doubt it will harm my research, so I see no reason to interfere in this particular squabble."

#. Key:	1320553709
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(184).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(184).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "Content,1320553709"
msgid "I admit, there are times when it is useful to live among simpletons. For example, I was able to trade several gallons of my Lazarus Chowder to a group of hunters in exchange for an entire contingent of tamed gigantopithecus, and they never questioned whether it had been tested on humans yet. \n\nWell, I suppose if they return with another batch of apes, then I'll know that Lazarus Chowder doesn't cause asphyxiation, won't I? It's not exactly a conclusive, scientific trial, but I suppose it will serve.\n\nUnfortunately, all these primitive primates have given Rockwell Manor quite the pungent odor. Isabelle said she is working on some sort of air freshener, but I hope she makes haste."
msgstr "I admit, there are times when it is useful to live among simpletons. For example, I was able to trade several gallons of my Lazarus Chowder to a group of hunters in exchange for an entire contingent of tamed gigantopithecus, and they never questioned whether it had been tested on humans yet. \n\nWell, I suppose if they return with another batch of apes, then I'll know that Lazarus Chowder doesn't cause asphyxiation, won't I? It's not exactly a conclusive, scientific trial, but I suppose it will serve.\n\nUnfortunately, all these primitive primates have given Rockwell Manor quite the pungent odor. Isabelle said she is working on some sort of air freshener, but I hope she makes haste."

#. Key:	212706096
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(251).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP.Default__COREMEDIA_PrimalGameData_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(251).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "Content,212706096"
msgid "As I expected, Rockwell couldn't deny my theory, but I can't say that I have his endorsement either. He didn't seem terribly engrossed in the subject, frankly. Something else seems to have captured his attention as of late – the Island's obelisks.\n\nApparently, Rockwell stumbled upon a way to interact with the towering monuments while spelunking, of all things. I guess he felt the need to scratch that old intrepid explorer itch of his. It's pretty impressive, considering his age.\n\nNow that I think about it, the obelisks could be linked to my own findings. Their nature has always been a mystery, and Rockwell made some intriguing observations. I should follow up."
msgstr "As I expected, Rockwell couldn't deny my theory, but I can't say that I have his endorsement either. He didn't seem terribly engrossed in the subject, frankly. Something else seems to have captured his attention as of late – the Island's obelisks.\n\nApparently, Rockwell stumbled upon a way to interact with the towering monuments while spelunking, of all things. I guess he felt the need to scratch that old intrepid explorer itch of his. It's pretty impressive, considering his age.\n\nNow that I think about it, the obelisks could be linked to my own findings. Their nature has always been a mystery, and Rockwell made some intriguing observations. I should follow up."

