#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1269).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,1977359039"
msgid "Species: Umbris phasmequester\r\nTime: Unknown\r\nDiet: Carrion Feeder\r\nTemperament: Aggressive near carcasses\r\n\r\nWild \r\nI’d have thought an apex predator like T. Rex or Giganotosaurus would be the scariest thing on the ARK, until I first saw this vision from a heavy metal album cover spread its wings. Dreadmare can induce an acute threat response in literally anything. All the better to scare away other scavengers from the dead meat it’s drawn to.\r\n\r\n\r\nThose wings can focus gusts to create pressure blasts at the point of impact. Dreadmare also has an uncanny way of disrupting a target’s healing abilities while boosting its own. And there’s no outnumbering this terror, since its dreadful aura seems to drain the will to live from everything around it. \r\n\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nYou aren’t going to break this beast the usual way. The only way to gain a Dreadmare’s respect is by killing it a few times. Yes, you read that right -- you will need to respawn one to fight again and again until you prove yourself worthy. \r\n\r\n\r\nOnce you’ve won its favor, your Dreadmare will reveal its greatest ability: to tuck another of your war-beasts into a pocket dimension for later access. Soon you’ll be riding into battle on a shadowy pegasus that can bring along surprise backup!\r\n"
msgstr "Species: Umbris phasmequester\r\nTime: Unknown\r\nDiet: Carrion Feeder\r\nTemperament: Aggressive near carcasses\r\n\r\nWild \r\nI’d have thought an apex predator like T. Rex or Giganotosaurus would be the scariest thing on the ARK, until I first saw this vision from a heavy metal album cover spread its wings. Dreadmare can induce an acute threat response in literally anything. All the better to scare away other scavengers from the dead meat it’s drawn to.\r\n\r\n\r\nThose wings can focus gusts to create pressure blasts at the point of impact. Dreadmare also has an uncanny way of disrupting a target’s healing abilities while boosting its own. And there’s no outnumbering this terror, since its dreadful aura seems to drain the will to live from everything around it. \r\n\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nYou aren’t going to break this beast the usual way. The only way to gain a Dreadmare’s respect is by killing it a few times. Yes, you read that right -- you will need to respawn one to fight again and again until you prove yourself worthy. \r\n\r\n\r\nOnce you’ve won its favor, your Dreadmare will reveal its greatest ability: to tuck another of your war-beasts into a pocket dimension for later access. Soon you’ll be riding into battle on a shadowy pegasus that can bring along surprise backup!\r\n"

#. Key:	635403703
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(127).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(127).ExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "Content,635403703"
msgid "Helena, you're a dipstick.\n\nGoing through my notes, I've realized that there are more predators than prey across this entire island by almost double. That's the opposite of how any ecosystem is supposed to work. I can't believe it took a Tyrannosaurus frolicking through the snow for me to see this. It's plain as day!\n\nWhat to make of it? Add in the human factor, and it's impossible for this island to continue as it is by natural means. So what, is this island's wildlife being monitored and curated somehow?\n\nI should speak with Rockwell. Maybe he's come to a similar conclusion."
msgstr "Helena, you're a dipstick.\n\nGoing through my notes, I've realized that there are more predators than prey across this entire island by almost double. That's the opposite of how any ecosystem is supposed to work. I can't believe it took a Tyrannosaurus frolicking through the snow for me to see this. It's plain as day!\n\nWhat to make of it? Add in the human factor, and it's impossible for this island to continue as it is by natural means. So what, is this island's wildlife being monitored and curated somehow?\n\nI should speak with Rockwell. Maybe he's come to a similar conclusion."

#. Key:	2414510689
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(0).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(0).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,2414510689"
msgid "Bob:  After all we’d gone through to get back to Earth, it was a real kick in the gut to see how dead the place was."
msgstr "Bob:  After all we’d gone through to get back to Earth, it was a real kick in the gut to see how dead the place was."

#. Key:	45318722
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(1).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(1).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,45318722"
msgid "Bob:  I hadn’t been there since WW2. We were seeing what was left after the final war."
msgstr "Bob:  I hadn’t been there since WW2. We were seeing what was left after the final war."

#. Key:	4008747756
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(2).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(2).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,4008747756"
msgid "Bob:  We got there too late to save anybody. Everything was in ruins. And there was no one around but ghosts."
msgstr "Bob:  We got there too late to save anybody. Everything was in ruins. And there was no one around but ghosts."

#. Key:	4262190950
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.ExplorerNoteEntries(1270).ExplorerNoteEntries.BinkMediaSubtitles(3).BinkMediaSubtitles.BaseText
