msgctxt "GraphLiteral,136233018"
msgid "Common Name: Aureliax\r\nSpecies: Draconis superbus\r\nTime: Necrocene\r\nDiet: Carnivore\r\nTemperament: Proudly Aloof\r\n\r\nOverview\r\nProject Aureliax was an early attempt to engineer an auspicious guardian for Arat Prime, obviously inspired by the legendary dragons of East Asia. These serpentine creatures were given a suite of telekinetic enhancements, including an eerie ability to levitate.\r\n\r\nOn our first sighting of a Titan rampaging through the post-Cataclysmic world at large, we realized these would-be protectors were overmatched and sealed them away with us under the Great Dome. But lately I find myself reevaluating the usefulness of Aureliax as airpower for our military forces.\r\n\r\nApplications\r\nEarning the trust of one of these supercilious serpents is a challenge... A Thrall must bring gifts to an Aureliax in order to prove their worth. Once satisfied with its tribute, the dragon will coil itself into an ovoid chrysalis to begin the imprinting process. This temporarily helpless egg-shaped bundle must be defended until it ‘hatches’ a newly-bonded Aureliax.\r\n\r\nAn Aureliax can carry multiple beasts of burden in its airborne coils and protect them with an array of celestial powers. Depending on their mood, they might breathe life or death, locally warp reality to help or hinder flying creatures, or raise icy pillars and spikes to throw allies or stab enemies.\r\n\r\nWhile not the most intimidating creature in our menagerie, an Aureliax is the envy of the earthbound.\r\n"
msgstr "Common Name: Aureliax\r\nSpecies: Draconis superbus\r\nTime: Necrocene\r\nDiet: Carnivore\r\nTemperament: Proudly Aloof\r\n\r\nOverview\r\nProject Aureliax was an early attempt to engineer an auspicious guardian for Arat Prime, obviously inspired by the legendary dragons of East Asia. These serpentine creatures were given a suite of telekinetic enhancements, including an eerie ability to levitate.\r\n\r\nOn our first sighting of a Titan rampaging through the post-Cataclysmic world at large, we realized these would-be protectors were overmatched and sealed them away with us under the Great Dome. But lately I find myself reevaluating the usefulness of Aureliax as airpower for our military forces.\r\n\r\nApplications\r\nEarning the trust of one of these supercilious serpents is a challenge... A Thrall must bring gifts to an Aureliax in order to prove their worth. Once satisfied with its tribute, the dragon will coil itself into an ovoid chrysalis to begin the imprinting process. This temporarily helpless egg-shaped bundle must be defended until it ‘hatches’ a newly-bonded Aureliax.\r\n\r\nAn Aureliax can carry multiple beasts of burden in its airborne coils and protect them with an array of celestial powers. Depending on their mood, they might breathe life or death, locally warp reality to help or hinder flying creatures, or raise icy pillars and spikes to throw allies or stab enemies.\r\n\r\nWhile not the most intimidating creature in our menagerie, an Aureliax is the envy of the earthbound.\r\n"

