msgctxt "GraphLiteral,194739721"
msgid "Common Name: Cryolophosaurus\r\nSpecies: Cryolophosaurus Glacialis\r\nTime: Early Jurassic\r\nDiet: Carnivore\r\nTemperament: Extremely Aggressive\r\n\r\nWild\r\nFor its small and seemingly innocent stature, Cryolophosaurus is one of the most dangerous creatures I've encountered on the ark. Cryo seems to possess a unique gular pouch that houses a potent freezing and tranquilizing agent. By intaking water or snow in its native habitat, Cryo can store this liquid and use it to \r\ndevastating effect; as tranquilizing spit, or a freezing gust of air. When subduing targets in this manner, Cryo seems to enter a hyper state displayed by vibrant flashing patterns and hyperventilating. This frenzied energy gives Cryo a significant boost in speed and power, which makes avoiding these debilitating attacks all the more crucial. Although they excel at tranquilizing targets, they themselves are not immune to the effects of torpor. While traditional methods will work but return weaker results, a well-armored survivor with shield in hand, is quite successful at giving a Cryo a taste of its' own cold \r\nmedicine.\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nTamed Cryolophosaurus are one of the most successful taming partners you could find, with torpor attacks that can cause even some of the strongest creatures to succumb to sleep. Its' freezing breath, while potent on enemies, also boasts a useful secondary benefit to allies. With a careful coating of this icy substance, allies will gain an icy coat of armor to help stave off damage. When hyper, Cryo can also assist in the chase by slowing down running targets with their chilling bites. While not quite able to stand as a powerhouse on its' own, Cryolophosaurus make for an excellent debilitating and status applying beast. As long as you're not afraid to get a little cold or sleepy..."
msgstr "Common Name: Cryolophosaurus\r\nSpecies: Cryolophosaurus Glacialis\r\nTime: Early Jurassic\r\nDiet: Carnivore\r\nTemperament: Extremely Aggressive\r\n\r\nWild\r\nFor its small and seemingly innocent stature, Cryolophosaurus is one of the most dangerous creatures I've encountered on the ark. Cryo seems to possess a unique gular pouch that houses a potent freezing and tranquilizing agent. By intaking water or snow in its native habitat, Cryo can store this liquid and use it to \r\ndevastating effect; as tranquilizing spit, or a freezing gust of air. When subduing targets in this manner, Cryo seems to enter a hyper state displayed by vibrant flashing patterns and hyperventilating. This frenzied energy gives Cryo a significant boost in speed and power, which makes avoiding these debilitating attacks all the more crucial. Although they excel at tranquilizing targets, they themselves are not immune to the effects of torpor. While traditional methods will work but return weaker results, a well-armored survivor with shield in hand, is quite successful at giving a Cryo a taste of its' own cold \r\nmedicine.\r\n\r\nDomesticated\r\nTamed Cryolophosaurus are one of the most successful taming partners you could find, with torpor attacks that can cause even some of the strongest creatures to succumb to sleep. Its' freezing breath, while potent on enemies, also boasts a useful secondary benefit to allies. With a careful coating of this icy substance, allies will gain an icy coat of armor to help stave off damage. When hyper, Cryo can also assist in the chase by slowing down running targets with their chilling bites. While not quite able to stand as a powerhouse on its' own, Cryolophosaurus make for an excellent debilitating and status applying beast. As long as you're not afraid to get a little cold or sleepy..."

