#. Key:	2341089138
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.NamedExplorerNoteEntries(5 - Value).NamedExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.NamedExplorerNoteEntries(5 - Value).NamedExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,2341089138"
msgid "I swear I can’t seem to catch a break, Janie.\r\nAlmost threw in with some folks building Swiss Family Robinson-style houses up in the trees. Getting above it all sure seemed like a great idea to me. But then I couldn’t help noticing this outfit was gearing up for a fight.\r\nIt was like boot camp all over again, except I don’t remember any Chinese lady sergeants there drilling recruits with pig-stickers. Besides, I wasn’t keen about enlisting in a brand-new war so soon after I’d gone AWOL from another.\r\nSo I struck out on my own, but not too far. Thought there might be something to that safety in numbers idea, in case those guys from the mine came back to make an example of us escapees. I spent a few days building a nice tree fort all my own, off to one side of Toothpick Terraces.\r\nNo sooner did I have my place all set up just the way I liked, when the bad guys showed up. I knew we were in for it when I saw they had artillery mounted on dinosaurs. And sure enough, they started raining hell on us! All that work for nothing...\r\nIn the middle of the mess I managed to spot the kid from the mine again, the one who broke us out. You’d think I would have learned by now to stick with her, but no. I heard her yelling to run into the swamps, and decided I might do better going the opposite way.\r\n\r\nAlready thinking I might’ve screwed up again -- BOB"
msgstr "I swear I can’t seem to catch a break, Janie.\r\nAlmost threw in with some folks building Swiss Family Robinson-style houses up in the trees. Getting above it all sure seemed like a great idea to me. But then I couldn’t help noticing this outfit was gearing up for a fight.\r\nIt was like boot camp all over again, except I don’t remember any Chinese lady sergeants there drilling recruits with pig-stickers. Besides, I wasn’t keen about enlisting in a brand-new war so soon after I’d gone AWOL from another.\r\nSo I struck out on my own, but not too far. Thought there might be something to that safety in numbers idea, in case those guys from the mine came back to make an example of us escapees. I spent a few days building a nice tree fort all my own, off to one side of Toothpick Terraces.\r\nNo sooner did I have my place all set up just the way I liked, when the bad guys showed up. I knew we were in for it when I saw they had artillery mounted on dinosaurs. And sure enough, they started raining hell on us! All that work for nothing...\r\nIn the middle of the mess I managed to spot the kid from the mine again, the one who broke us out. You’d think I would have learned by now to stick with her, but no. I heard her yelling to run into the swamps, and decided I might do better going the opposite way.\r\n\r\nAlready thinking I might’ve screwed up again -- BOB"

#. Key:	892247345
#. SourceLocation:	/Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.NamedExplorerNoteEntries(6 - Value).NamedExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
#: /Game/PrimalEarth/CoreBlueprints/PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP.Default__PrimalGameDataARKNX_BP_C.NamedExplorerNoteEntries(6 - Value).NamedExplorerNoteEntries.LocalizedSubtitle
msgctxt "GraphLiteral,892247345"
msgid "Dear Janie, I definitely made a big mistake running away from everyone else from Treehouse Company. And that’s not just cause I ended up running straight back to where the bad guys came from. I’m also realizing how much harder it is to get by out here on my own.\r\nI’ve been stuck behind enemy lines, trying to survive off whatever scraps I can scrounge outside that stone fortress of theirs. After a day or so of watching some of the local thieving rat-lizards sneak in and out of the fort like it was nothing, I thought I’d rob them instead. Better to let the critters take all the risk, I figured.\r\nI was all set to spear one when a bomb went off inside the fortress! The blast wave knocked me right off my feet, and that whiskery little bastard ran off with his haul of carrots before I even could think of going after him.\r\nDidn’t have much time for bellyaching before I heard a roar like none other, that sent a shiver right down my spine.b Couldn’t tell what the hell was going down in there, but I know a fight to the death when I hear one.\r\nI was all set to play soldier one last time and charge into battle, but something exploded inside the fort and collapsed my only way in. I just hope that any good guys in that scrap were OK.\r\nFor now, I think I’m gonna take a long breather, and stop getting involved in one snafu after another. ‘Sides, I think I see that thieving rat-lizard again, and it looks like it’s carrying an... axe?\r\nSomething mighty familiar about that axe...\r\n\r\nYours forever -- BOB"
msgstr "Dear Janie, I definitely made a big mistake running away from everyone else from Treehouse Company. And that’s not just cause I ended up running straight back to where the bad guys came from. I’m also realizing how much harder it is to get by out here on my own.\r\nI’ve been stuck behind enemy lines, trying to survive off whatever scraps I can scrounge outside that stone fortress of theirs. After a day or so of watching some of the local thieving rat-lizards sneak in and out of the fort like it was nothing, I thought I’d rob them instead. Better to let the critters take all the risk, I figured.\r\nI was all set to spear one when a bomb went off inside the fortress! The blast wave knocked me right off my feet, and that whiskery little bastard ran off with his haul of carrots before I even could think of going after him.\r\nDidn’t have much time for bellyaching before I heard a roar like none other, that sent a shiver right down my spine.b Couldn’t tell what the hell was going down in there, but I know a fight to the death when I hear one.\r\nI was all set to play soldier one last time and charge into battle, but something exploded inside the fort and collapsed my only way in. I just hope that any good guys in that scrap were OK.\r\nFor now, I think I’m gonna take a long breather, and stop getting involved in one snafu after another. ‘Sides, I think I see that thieving rat-lizard again, and it looks like it’s carrying an... axe?\r\nSomething mighty familiar about that axe...\r\n\r\nYours forever -- BOB"

